<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piet Mondrian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1872–1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Piet Mondriaan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piet Mondrian was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> painter and a pioneer of abstract art. With Theo van Doesburg he founded the De Stijl movement in 1917, and he developed Neo-Plasticism, painting grids of black lines with blocks of primary colours on white. His work strongly influenced modern design and architecture. He lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and from 1940 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piet-mondrian.jpg" alt="Piet Mondrian" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piet_Mondriaan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
